          "quote": "+5V : C2.1(passive) J3.1(Pin_1,passive) J4.2(VCC,passive) J6.2(Pin_2,passive) R3.1(passive) U1.2(VO,power_out) U2.8(VCC,power_in) U3.8(VCC,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both listed MCUs are assembled, their outputs share the fan-control and interface nets. Differences in firmware state or timing can cause output contention and unreliable fan control or programming. The files do not indicate that one MCU is an unpopulated alternative.",
      "confidence": 0.76
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist connects two different ATtiny MCUs in parallel across their signals, reset, and supply. Unless the footprints are intended as mutually exclusive alternatives, populating both risks contention on shared outputs."
}

